[gd_resource type="Theme" load_steps=20 format=3]

; Light "parchment" palette, ported directly from the reference HTML's own
; `:root[data-theme="light"]` block (Cartalith Gen1 v2.10.html, line 271) --
; not a fresh ui-ux-pro-max match, a literal port of the reference app's real
; alternate theme (itself ported from the V1.915 editor's "Light" palette).
; The reference's own comment there is worth repeating: this restyles UI
; chrome only, never the rendered map (JS colour ramps, not CSS) -- ported
; here in that same spirit, this Theme resource only ever touches Godot
; Control styling, never `render.rs`'s pixel output.
;
;   bg #efe7d6  panel #fbf5e9  panel2 #e7ddc9  line #d3c8b0
;   ink #2a2015 (primary text)   dim #6d5f47 (secondary)   faint #9a8b70
;   accent #b07f3f (warm brown, reference's own primary highlight colour)
;   accent2 #3f6f9e (blue, used here only for keyboard-focus rings, so
;   "focused" reads distinct from "primary/active" accent styling)
;   warn #b04a4a
;
; Superseded 2026-08-16 dark "technical dashboard" ui-ux-pro-max match
; (background #0F172A / accent #22C55E) per explicit user preference for
; the reference app's own light scheme instead.
;
; Font: kept Godot's built-in default (Fira Sans/Fira Code was the earlier
; dark-theme pass's typography match; sourcing + licensing real font files
; is still a deferred follow-up, see CHANGELOG.md).

